# No Back Buttons

- Do not introduce explicit "Back", "Back to List", or similar navigation buttons in page headers or content areas.
- Prefer existing global navigation patterns (sidebar, breadcrumbs, browser/app navigation).
- When updating existing UI, remove newly added back buttons unless the user explicitly asks for one.

## Example

- Avoid: an `ActionButton` with back arrow that routes to a previous list page.
- Prefer: no extra button; keep header actions focused on page-specific operations.
